import json
from pathlib import Path
root=Path('content-reserve');root.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
data=[
('Repair records and hidden failures',[
'In 2022, the fictional town of Mereford opened a repair desk for small household appliances. Volunteers recorded the item, its apparent fault and the outcome of each attempted repair. The council initially wanted to use the records to estimate the proportion of all broken appliances that could be repaired locally. However, an analyst pointed out that people who attended the desk had selected themselves. Owners of very cheap items might discard them without visiting, while owners of expensive equipment might use commercial services.',
'The desk therefore began publishing a narrower measure: successful repairs as a proportion of items actually examined. It also recorded cases in which a fault could not be diagnosed. Previously these cases had been excluded, making the success rate appear higher. A separate note identified repairs delayed because replacement parts were unavailable. This distinction helped volunteers separate a lack of technical skill from a lack of suitable supplies.',
'After six months, visitors reported that learning how to maintain an appliance was valuable even when the immediate repair failed. The desk added optional maintenance demonstrations, but did not count attendance as a successful repair. The analyst argued that recording different benefits separately made the report more informative. The project had not established whether it reduced appliance purchases across the town; answering that question would require evidence about households that never used the service.'
],[('The original records represented every household in Mereford.','False',0,'people who attended the desk had selected themselves'),('Undiagnosed faults had previously been left out of the calculation.','True',1,'Previously these cases had been excluded'),('The maintenance demonstrations reduced visitors’ energy bills.','Not Given',2,'added optional maintenance demonstrations')],[('The published repair rate now covered items actually _____.','examined',1),('Some repairs were delayed by unavailable replacement _____.','parts',1),('The desk offered optional maintenance _____.','demonstrations',2)]),
('A seed collection with missing stories',[
'At a fictional regional garden, staff discovered a box of seeds collected during a survey forty years earlier. Labels gave dates and locations, but rarely described how many plants had been sampled. The collection was potentially useful for studying change, yet it could not be assumed to represent the full diversity of the original populations. A single productive plant might have supplied most seeds in an envelope.',
'Before attempting large-scale germination, the curator set aside a small sample from each envelope for a pilot test. The aim was to learn which storage histories were associated with survival while preserving material for later work. Seeds that did not germinate were not automatically classified as dead: some species require a period of cold or other environmental signals before growth begins. The team tested several treatments and documented them individually.',
'Local residents supplied photographs and notebooks describing the survey. These sources clarified some collection routes, although memories sometimes disagreed with written dates. The curator retained both accounts with an explanation of the discrepancy instead of choosing whichever seemed more convenient. The project could reveal which surviving seeds responded to particular treatments. It could not reconstruct all the genetic variation that had existed in the landscape forty years earlier.'
],[('The labels usually stated how many plants had been sampled.','False',0,'rarely described how many plants had been sampled'),('Failure to germinate always proved that a seed was dead.','False',1,'not automatically classified as dead'),('Every resident had participated in the original survey.','Not Given',2,'Local residents supplied photographs and notebooks')],[('The curator first conducted a small _____ test.','pilot',1),('Some species need a period of _____ before growth begins.','cold',1),('Residents provided photographs and _____.','notebooks',2)]),
('The bus timetable experiment',[
'The fictional city of Renwick tested a revised bus timetable on two routes. Instead of adding departures, planners moved several departures to match shift changes at a hospital. Passenger numbers increased during the first month. The transport office cautioned that the month also included roadworks that made driving less convenient. Comparing passenger totals before and after the change alone would not separate these effects.',
'Researchers therefore examined a third route where the timetable had remained unchanged. This comparison was useful but imperfect: the third route served a college, whose term dates affected demand. The team reported the different contexts rather than treating the comparison as a controlled experiment. Interviews with hospital staff suggested that a reliable connection mattered more to some workers than a small reduction in journey time.',
'The office retained the revised timetable for another three months and began collecting information about missed connections. It published departure reliability separately from passenger satisfaction, since a crowded but punctual bus might receive low comfort ratings. The findings supported continued monitoring, rather than a claim that moving departures would work equally well across the whole network. No fare changes were introduced during the pilot, and the report did not estimate the cost of extending the scheme.'
],[('The pilot increased the number of departures.','False',0,'Instead of adding departures'),('The comparison route served a college.','True',1,'the third route served a college'),('The report calculated the cost of a city-wide extension.','False',2,'did not estimate the cost of extending the scheme')],[('Departures were adjusted to match hospital shift _____.','changes',0),('Driving was less convenient because of _____.','roadworks',0),('Researchers collected information about missed _____.','connections',2)]),
('When a museum changes a label',[
'A fictional museum at Ashcombe rewrote labels in its geology gallery after visitors said that unfamiliar terminology made the displays difficult to follow. The first draft replaced technical words with everyday descriptions. A curator warned that removing every specialist term would prevent visitors from learning the vocabulary needed to explore the subject further. The final version retained key terms and explained them through examples.',
'The museum compared two versions of a label beside the same mineral display on alternate days. Staff asked visitors to explain the main process in their own words rather than merely say whether they liked the text. Responses suggested that a short example helped people describe the process. However, the groups were not randomly assigned, and weekend visitors often included more families. Staff treated the result as a reason to refine the labels, not as definitive proof of a universal design rule.',
'An audio description was added for visitors who preferred listening. Its script included details that could be felt on a replica, which visitors were permitted to touch. The museum kept a record of label revisions so that later evaluations could identify exactly what had changed. It had not tested whether visitors remembered the explanations several weeks later. The team planned a follow-up study but recognised that people willing to return might differ from other visitors.'
],[('The final labels removed all specialist vocabulary.','False',0,'retained key terms'),('Visitors were asked to explain a process in their own words.','True',1,'explain the main process in their own words'),('Most visitors preferred audio to written labels.','Not Given',2,'visitors who preferred listening')],[('Label versions were shown on alternate _____.','days',1),('Visitors could touch a _____.','replica',2),('The museum recorded label _____.','revisions',2)])]
for n,(title,pars,checks,fills) in enumerate(data,1):
 pid=f'weekly-r-{n}';qs=[]
 for i,(prompt,ans,par,evidence) in enumerate(checks):qs.append(dict(id=f'{pid}-q{i+1}',type='select',prompt='True / False / Not Given: '+prompt,answers=[ans],options=['True','False','Not Given'],evidence=evidence,explanation='对照所引原文：明确相反信息判 False，原文未提供比较或因果证据判 Not Given；支持题干则判 True。'))
 for i,(prompt,ans,par) in enumerate(fills):qs.append(dict(id=f'{pid}-q{i+4}',type='text',prompt='Complete with ONE WORD: '+prompt,answers=[ans],maxWords=1,evidence=pars[par],explanation='根据题干关键词定位原文，抄取符合句法和单词数限制的对应词：'+ans+'。'))
 paper=dict(id=pid,skill='reading',title=title,subtitle='每周专项 · 证据与研究边界',minutes=12,source='本站原创 / AI 辅助编写，机构与研究情境均为虚构。',kind='原创练习',review='教学练习，未人工考官审定、未标准化校准。',updated='2026-11-16',difficulty='B2 目标阅读训练，非实测等级。',passages=[dict(id=pid+'-p1',title=title,paragraphs=[dict(label=chr(65+i),text=t) for i,t in enumerate(pars)],questions=qs)])
 (root/f'batch-{n:03}.json').write_text(json.dumps([paper],ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
if not (root/'released.json').exists():(root/'released.json').write_text('[]\n')
